    "abstract": null,
    "field": "Attribution of weather-related disaster impacts",
    "problem": "The paper addresses the challenge of isolating the influence of climate change on weather-related disasters, since the overall disaster burden is also heavily influenced by confounding socioeconomic drivers such as growth in population and wealth, and changes in vulnerability.",
    "method": "This paper proposes a method that normalizes weather-related disaster impacts for population and wealth changes, followed by a trend analysis of the normalized data to compare with trends in climate drivers and vulnerability, thereby isolating the role of climate change.",
    "task": "The task is to determine the influence of climate change on weather-related disaster impacts by normalizing disaster data and comparing trends in impacts, extreme weather events, and vulnerability.",
